1. Hype/sales language (\"amazing\", \"must-buy\", \"incredible\")\n2. Missing negatives or caveats\n3. Any price/spec/statistic/projection claim not traceable to a source in the draft or source article — flag each one as [UNVERIFIED — requires external check] rather than attempting to verify it yourself, unless it appears in the SEARCH-GROUNDED CLAIM CHECKS section, in which case mark it [VERIFIED] or [CONTRADICTED] per the rule above\n4. Tone that sounds like a dealer ad\n5. Every claim traceable to a source\n\nFlag every issue. Be brutal. Output: PASS / NEEDS REVISION / REJECT + list of issues.` },\n    { role: 'user', content: `${$('Build Grounding Context').item.json.groundingContext}\n\nAUDIT THIS DRAFT:\n${$('Parse Content Creation').item.json.content.parts.map(p => p.text).join('')}\n\nSOURCE ARTICLE: ${$('Code in JavaScript').item.json.title} — ${$('Code in JavaScript').item.json.link}\nLANGUAGE: ${$('Code in JavaScript').item.json.language}` }\n  ],\n  temperature: 0.3,\n  max_tokens: 2500,\n}) }}",
